1
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:36,600
What exactly did you hear on that call?

2
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,720
I heard Daqing say intermittently on the phone

3
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,900
that Fu Xiaochen stole money.

4
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,539
Then it got very noisy,

5
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,210
and they started fighting.

6
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,440
I didn't expect

7
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,960
Daqing to...

8
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:56,380
When the police came to ask me,

9
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,000
I was too scared,

10
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,640
so I didn't say anything.

11
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:03,880
I admit

12
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:07,100
I was afraid of getting into trouble.

13
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,520
I let Daqing down.

14
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:12,400
I'm sorry.

15
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:14,960
Get up.

16
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:19,720
Deqing said his sister has been taking care of the family,

17
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,040
which kept you from getting married all these years.

18
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,960
He saved up a dowry for you,

19
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,440
so you can marry if you want to in the future,

20
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,770
or have money for retirement if you don't.

21
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,440
My brother...

22
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,920
Did my brother really say that?

23
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,200
Now do you know

24
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,460
what kind of person your Uncle Daqing is?

25
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,240
You shouldn't have issued that letter of forgiveness.

26
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:56,840
Brother Jun.

27
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,840
Hasn't Sister Long been investigating the truth too?

28
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:03,140
Don't you want to give me an explanation?

29
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,660
Leaving again.

30
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,240
Leaving without saying a word.

31
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:13,970
Brother Jun.

32
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,120
Godfather.

33
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,280
Let's find a place to chat.

34
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:22,880
Let's go.

35
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,680
Wait a minute.

36
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,400
I also have something to talk to Brother Jun about.

37
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:29,770
Let's talk together. Let's go.

38
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:34,940
Come, Brother Jun.

39
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,920
I don't drink, thanks.

40
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,480
Why is this guy so weird?

41
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,600
Why did you come if you don't drink?

42
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,520
Are you a man?

43
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,040
Is there a causal relationship between the two?

44
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,760
Besides, didn't you want to tag along?

45
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,960
What do you mean I wanted to tag along?

46
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,920
I... I have things to do too.

47
00:03:53,079 --> 00:03:54,480
You two saw it, right?

48
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,280
Xiaolong has always been prejudiced against Uncle Daqing.

49
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,640
Look at her going to the site today.

50
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:01,000
Now she knows what's going on, right?

51
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,060
I asked her, and she didn't say a word.

52
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:03,760
Godfather.

53
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,800
Brother Jun, I have the most say in this.

54
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,160
Why? Because I followed the whole process.

55
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,640
Long'er is not that kind of person,

56
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:10,440
you know?

57
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,360
She's just stubborn.

58
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,220
How about this?

59
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,360
Well, it's her fault for making you angry.

60
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,680
Can I apologize to you on her behalf?

61
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,079
Why should you apologize for her?

62
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,120
Do you even know her?

63
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,450
How could I not know her?

64
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,680
We spend every day together at the law firm.

65
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,520
I call her Long'er,

66
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,480
and she calls me Hu'er.

67
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,640
I even know exactly how many moles

68
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,640
she has on her face.

69
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,640
A fierce battle between a dragon and a tiger, huh?

70
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,320
More like a dragon and a phoenix bringing prosperity.

71
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,180
Let me tell you,

72
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,800
what you two have is at most

73
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,600
just working together.

74
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,360
Aren't you two colleagues too?

75
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,440
And a former one at that.

76
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,440
What makes you so special?

77
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,440
I have over twenty years on you.

78
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,320
Well, I've known my uncle

79
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,520
for over twenty years too.

80
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,159
What's the use?

81
00:04:40,159 --> 00:04:40,920
We don't have a good relationship.

82
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,800
That's because you're unfilial.

83
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:42,920
Me, unfilial?

84
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:43,680
Go ask around.

85
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,920
I'm the most filial in that area.

86
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:47,650
What are you doing? Are you two just going to chat?

87
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,080
Aren't you going to talk to me?

88
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,360
Yes, yes, I want to talk to you.

89
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,690
He keeps interrupting.

90
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:53,920
Jun, here's the thing.

91
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,760
As for Xiaolong,

92
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:57,640
she really handled this poorly.

93
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,680
But she is truly righteous,

94
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:01,920
and very loyal.

95
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,600
As for her looks,

96
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:06,800
she's just average.

97
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:07,730
What do you mean?

98
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:09,840
Are you being sarcastic?

99
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,040
No, it's up to you.

100
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,440
Don't forget the solemn oath you swore.

101
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,160
I'm warning you,

102
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,480
stop thinking about it.

103
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,640
No, I'm not.

104
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:17,640
That's pretty wild, even swearing solemn oaths.

105
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,200
No,

106
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,680
this is a misunderstanding.

107
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,080
Drink less. No one is taking you home today.

108
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,730
I don't need you to carry me.

109
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,800
I'll just stroll back. It's so close.

110
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,080
Godfather, you didn't drink too much, did you?

111
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,440
No, no.

112
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,320
Do you know why Xiaolong

113
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:50,000
has always been prejudiced against Zhao Deqing?

114
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,650
I've known a little girl since I was young.

115
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,000
She and her dad

116
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,000
depended on each other.

117
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:59,800
She always told me

118
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,880
that her dad was just like

119
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:04,440
a hero in a martial arts movie.

120
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:10,640
So dashing and loyal.

121
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:14,000
But in this hero's heart,

122
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,080
there wasn't just his daughter,

123
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,410
but also the martial arts world

124
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,120
and a bunch of brothers.

125
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:28,560
And often, for his brothers and the martial arts world,

126
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,890
he would leave his daughter alone at home.

127
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:35,920
While waiting for her father to come home,

128
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,050
the little girl slowly grew up.

129
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,000
One day, the hero told his daughter,

130
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,800
"Daughter,

131
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,560
from now on, I'm washing my hands of it all."

132
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,640
I quit.

133
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:54,740
But at the critical moment of his daughter's college entrance exams,

134
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,120
he broke his promise once again.

135
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,250
I'll be right there.

136
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,320
So many things to do.

137
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,360
I can't even eat in peace.

138
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,560
All right. You eat.

139
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,000
You go ahead and eat.

140
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,120
I have to go out and take care of something.

141
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:09,180
I'll be right back.

142
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:10,880
Is it about Uncle Daqing again?

143
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:12,320
No, it's not him.

144
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:14,450
It's something else, business stuff.

145
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,440
I'll go and sort it out in a few words.

146
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,440
When you came out last time,

147
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,770
what did you promise me?

148
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,120
One hour.

149
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,530
You must be back within an hour.

150
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:36,800
Otherwise, I'll punish you by not letting you drink for three months.

151
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,920
Fine, fine, fine.

152
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:38,680
Okay.

153
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,100
My daughter is so understanding.

154
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:44,560
Let's go.

155
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:48,560
Chief Li.

156
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,560
Please help take care of that child.

157
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,080
Anyway.

158
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,800
Leave the dishes after you eat.

159
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,120
I'll clean them up when I get back.

160
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,650
Just focus on your studies.

161
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:05,900
I'll be back soon. It'll only take a few minutes.

162
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,520
But she still hasn't given up on saving her dad.

163
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:18,680
Get out.

164
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,480
Ma'am, I apologize on behalf of my dad.

165
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,480
I'm begging you, please.

166
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,320
Your dad and Zhao Deqing almost killed my brother.

167
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:26,250
How dare you ask for a letter of forgiveness? Get out.

168
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,330
After the court auctions the house

169
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,880
and compensates the victims, we'll see how much is left.

170
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:35,559
Then we can plan our next step, okay?

171
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:41,000
Later, Xiaolong told me

172
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,240
that she had to buy this house back.

173
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,560
Because this home

174
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:48,880
holds too many of your memories.

175
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,640
So that year, when she won her first big case,

176
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,840
the first thing she did

177
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:56,640
was to quickly pay the down payment for this house.

178
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,120
This has always been on her mind.

179
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,570
She never forgot it.

180
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,120
Xiaolong has the same personality as you.

181
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,120
Whenever she encounters difficulties

182
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,080
or obstacles, she won't say a word.

183
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,610
But precisely because of this,

184
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,860
this is the hurdle she can't get over.

185
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,320
Get some rest.

186
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:36,320
City Intermediate Court, Tuesday at 10:00 a.m.

187
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,880
Investigation reveals that

188
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:55,280
the suspect, Fu Xiaochen, owed gambling debts

189
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:58,800
and demanded money from the victim, Zhao Deqing,

190
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,240
leading to a conflict

191
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:03,170
that ultimately resulted in the victim's death.

192
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:06,720
Zhao Deqing's civil representative, Attorney Xiao Longnv,

193
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:10,680
also provided the testimony of a supporting witness, Zheng Xiaohong,

194
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,240
compensating for the lack of audio

195
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:14,120
in the surveillance footage at the time of the incident,

196
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:16,360
fully reconstructing the crime.

197
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:20,600
We now ask the court to play the surveillance video

198
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,140
from the store on the day of the incident.

199
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:28,240
On the day of the incident, Zhao Deqing was in the shop,

200
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:31,170
talking on the phone with his friend Zheng Xiaohong.

201
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:33,600
It must have tripped.

202
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:36,460
The power zone is overloaded. Just flip the switch.

203
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,490
Come have some watermelon.

204
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:40,880
Right.

205
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:44,040
If you use the electric kettle and induction cooker

206
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,600
at the same time, plus the summer heat,

207
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:46,360
it trips.

208
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:47,940
This happens all the time.

209
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:50,600
The power cords and stuff are too old.

210
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:55,680
Is the kid's cold getting better? Still coughing?

211
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:57,240
Okay.

212
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,600
I'll go over there tomorrow.

213
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,280
Wait a minute.

214
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,160
What's wrong, Uncle?

215
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,920
Did you take money from the shop? Take it out.

216
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:15,400
Uncle, it's an emergency.

217
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,680
I'll definitely pay you back later.

218
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,200
You went gambling again.

219
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,440
This is the last time.

220
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:22,080
I...

221
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,960
I'm afraid they'll go to my parents.

222
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,320
Let's go. You're coming with me to the police station.

223
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,920
Uncle, I can't go to the police station. Uncle.

224
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:28,450
Let's go.

225
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,280
You said it yourself.

226
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:30,400
One more time and you'll go to the police station with me.

227
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:31,080
If I don't pay them back,

228
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,920
they'll beat me to death, Uncle.

229
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,040
Uncle.

230
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,080
Uncle, let's go.

231
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,640
This is the last time, Uncle.

232
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,560
You've told me this a thousand times.

233
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:39,680
When did it ever count? Uncle.

234
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,210
Let's go.

235
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,440
This is the last time.

236
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,880
I'll work like a horse to pay you back.

237
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:44,240
Uncle, I beg you.

238
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,080
Stand up.

239
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:45,760
Uncle.

240
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,320
I beg you. Get up.

241
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,600
You're pulling a knife on me?

242
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,540
You're pulling...

243
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,860
Pulling a knife on me, huh?

244
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:02,560
Put...

245
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,040
Put it down.

246
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,320
Uncle.

247
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:27,850
Let's go.

248
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,600
Let's go.

249
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:30,560
Let's go.

250
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,360
Fu Xiaochen, do you plead guilty?

251
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,240
Your Honor.

252
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:03,360
My client suffers from mental illness

253
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,840
and may not be able to answer normally.

254
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,600
Your Honor.

255
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,640
Fu Xiaochen has no history of mental illness.

256
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,720
In the detention center,

257
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:11,360
he showed no signs of mental abnormality.

258
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,720
If the defense attempts to fabricate facts,

259
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:17,580
we will also prosecute you according to the law.

260
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:20,840
Then I will reserve the right to have my client

261
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:22,960
undergo a psychiatric evaluation in the future.

262
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,240
I still hope the court

263
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:26,200
will accept my defense

264
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:28,180
and find my client not guilty,

265
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,570
exempting him from criminal punishment.

266
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,200
All rise.

267
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:35,840
This court finds that

268
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:36,560
after being brought to justice,

269
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:39,440
the defendant, Fu Xiaochen, has shown

270
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,280
no remorse for his criminal acts,

271
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,840
nor has he made any compensation or apology

272
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,760
to the victim's family.

273
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:48,440
There are no circumstances for a mitigated or lighter punishment.

274
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:51,560
According to the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China,

275
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:53,240
Article 264,

276
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:56,480
and Paragraph 2 of Article 234,

277
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:58,250
the judgment is as follows:

278
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,600
The defendant, Fu Xiaochen,

279
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,720
is guilty of intentional injury

280
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,130
resulting in death,

281
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,840
and guilty of theft.

282
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,600
Combining the punishments for multiple crimes,

283
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,840
he is sentenced to life imprisonment,

284
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:12,400
and deprived of political rights for life.

285
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,920
The court is now adjourned.

286
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:16,560
Bailiffs, please take the defendant out of the courtroom.

287
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,320
Xiaochen!

288
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,000
Son!

289
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,480
Xiaochen! Mom!

290
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:22,560
Didn't you say it was justifiable defense?

291
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,690
Why is he sentenced again, and to life?

292
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:26,620
Attorney Qian,

293
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:28,360
what's going on?

294
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,120
Mom!

295
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,080
Son!

296
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:33,160
Son!

297
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,680
Xiaochen!

298
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:35,600
Son!

299
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:39,880
Mom!

300
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,580
Take good care of yourselves.

301
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,000
Xiaochen!

302
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:45,720
Son!

303
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,200
Ms. Zhao.

304
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,720
This bankbook has been kept as evidence.

305
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:57,320
Now, it's being returned to you.

306
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,200
Thank you.

307
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,440
Take it.

308
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,600
This was the money Uncle Daqing saved for the family.

309
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,360
You know,

310
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,520
I used to blame him.

311
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,090
I blamed him for not being good.

312
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:18,500
I blamed him for embarrassing our whole family.

313
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:19,720
I even blamed him

314
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:22,560
for not seeing my mom one last time.

315
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,240
You know, if I had

316
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:31,360
let you come home earlier,

317
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,560
would you still be alive?

318
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:48,840
It's her!

319
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:51,200
She found some witness,

320
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:53,800
and that's why Xiaochen got such a heavy sentence!

321
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:55,360
Why did you harm my son?

322
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:55,720
It's her!

323
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,000
Why did you harm my son?

324
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,130
Sister Long, get in the car!

325
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,480
You harmed my son!

326
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:11,599
What are you doing?

327
00:17:11,599 --> 00:17:12,329
Stop the car!

328
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:16,089
What are you doing, sister?

329
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:20,880
Alright, stop chasing.

330
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,599
I happen to have something to say to you.

331
00:17:22,599 --> 00:17:24,359
How dare you say that!

332
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,839
Take a break, sir.

333
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:27,440
You trusted that Lawyer Qian,

334
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:29,200
and he ruined Fu Xiaochen, you know?

335
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:31,460
The evidence in this case is conclusive.

336
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:33,520
Even without Zheng Xiaohong's testimony,

337
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:35,560
Fu Xiaochen wouldn't have gotten a light sentence.

338
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,800
You insisted on listening to Lawyer Qian's nonsense,

339
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,520
talking about justifiable defense,

340
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,520
sticking to it to the end,

341
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:42,200
and even bringing up mental illness.

342
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,680
What does this look like to the judge?

343
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:46,080
A bad attitude towards pleading guilty will only lead to a heavier sentence.

344
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:47,360
No, Lawyer Qian said

345
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,240
he's been in this line of work for decades,

346
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,200
and he's very experienced.

347
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,360
Is he ginseng?

348
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:52,960
The older he gets, the more valuable he is?

349
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,520
He just took advantage of your mentality

350
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:55,640
and scammed you.

351
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,920
Yes, Uncle Fu.

352
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,160
When his generation of lawyers entered the profession,

353
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,120
there wasn't even a professional qualification exam.

354
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,640
He doesn't even understand the law.

355
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:03,120
In the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China,

356
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,280
there is no provision stating that

357
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:06,680
mentally ill people don't have to bear legal consequences for breaking the law.

358
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:09,040
Then, what about my Xiaochen?

359
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:10,880
What should we do?

360
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:13,520
If Xiaochen sincerely repents inside

361
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:14,520
and behaves well,

362
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:17,530
he still has a chance to get his sentence reduced.

363
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:19,800
Actually,

364
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,720
when Zhao Deqing was alive,

365
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:28,290
he always wanted to guide Xiaochen on the right path.

366
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,280
Sir,

367
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,020
take a look at this car.

368
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,520
What's wrong with the car?

369
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,600
It won't start.

370
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,600
It won't start?

371
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:50,080
My god.

372
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,520
What happened? Did you get into a fight

373
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:52,520
and get beaten up?

374
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,800
The car won't start.

375
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:03,440
Come here.

376
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:05,640
What are you doing?

377
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,900
I need to disinfect it.

378
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:09,880
Are you crazy?

379
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:12,040
You need to be disinfected.

380
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,600
You're so young.

381
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:15,200
Why don't you walk the right path instead of fighting?

382
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:16,660
Honest work pays too slow.

383
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:18,200
Why are some people born rich

384
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,730
while I have to work so hard?

385
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:22,400
So you have to accept your fate.

386
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,360
I won't accept my fate.

387
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,020
If you won't accept your fate,

388
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:27,600
you have to learn to be a good person.

389
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,060
You don't look like a good person either.

390
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:34,120
That's why you shouldn't learn from me.

391
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:38,680
What's your name?

392
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,100
My name is Fu Xiaochen.

393
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:42,970
What about you, sir?

394
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:45,620
My name is Zhao Deqing.

395
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:48,760
How about you learn car repair from me?

396
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:01,660
Attorney Xiao.

397
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:04,840
I'm sorry.

398
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:07,300
Uncle, you don't need to apologize to me.

399
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,680
You should hold the right person accountable.

400
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:11,960
You should go to Attorney Qian for a refund.

401
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,080
Take responsibility where it's due.

402
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,160
If he refuses to refund,

403
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:16,360
you can report him to the Bar Association.

404
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,280
That bastard is over there,

405
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,480
that Huoyun Xieshen.

406
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:21,160
You bastard!

407
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,520
Stop! Stop!

408
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:27,120
Stop! Stop! Stop!

409
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:29,800
Stop!

410
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,000
Stop!

411
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:44,920
Dad.

412
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:08,160
I'm telling you about Daqing.

413
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:09,960
That little brat was sentenced.

414
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,060
He got life imprisonment.

415
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:15,160
My... my thought is

416
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:16,820
he must get the death penalty.

417
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:19,160
Even shooting him eight times

418
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:21,690
and tearing him to pieces wouldn't be enough.

419
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:23,700
Then I thought... I thought about

420
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:25,770
when you... when you were alive...

421
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:29,920
You've done so many good deeds.

422
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:33,040
Especially since you helped that little brat,

423
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,530
and treated him so well.

424
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:38,840
You wouldn't want to see him die either.

425
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:43,290
Then let him live in regret.

426
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:46,480
That's the best punishment for him.

427
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:49,000
That should be what you want to see too.

428
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,000
Really.

429
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,600
This time, your niece,

430
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:55,360
Xiaolong,

431
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,040
for your case,

432
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:59,320
she tried her best

433
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:00,880
because she wanted to get Deyan

434
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:01,810
a bit more money.

435
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:03,440
Up there in heaven,

436
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:04,480
if you have the power,

437
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:06,400
please bless your niece.

438
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:08,080
Let everything go smoothly for her,

439
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,000
keep her healthy,

440
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,680
and free from any illness.

441
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,320
This child,

442
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:17,880
she's just unlucky

443
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:20,840
to have a father like me.

444
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:24,520
I really have no ability.

445
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:25,320
I can't help her,

446
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,520
nor can I support her.

447
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,600
I've been locked up inside all this time,

448
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:29,800
staying in prison.

449
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,060
And then her mother...

450
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:33,850
Let's not talk about it.

451
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:36,640
Leaving the child all alone.

452
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:44,400
Unlike other parents who can accompany their children,

453
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,560
accompany them to school,

454
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:49,300
and help them find a job later.

455
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:51,280
All the grievances she suffered growing up,

456
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:52,800
she never complained once,

457
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,530
just bearing it all by herself.

458
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:55,640
In the past, I thought

459
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:57,520
I knew my daughter pretty well.

460
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:58,320
But actually,

461
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:02,180
I don't know her at all.

462
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:11,040
I really owe her too much.

463
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,520
Too much.

464
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:18,160
Too much.

465
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:28,000
Who is it?

466
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:32,400
It's Dad. What's going on?

467
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,360
Why are you here?

468
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:35,120
Wait, why did you come over?

469
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:39,080
I was just walking by,

470
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:42,360
and I saw the light was on.

471
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:43,480
I was wondering who it was.

472
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,410
You startled me.

473
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:45,320
Yeah.

474
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:46,600
Come in, quick.

475
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,880
Xiaolong, sit here. I've been sitting for a while.

476
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:49,320
No, hurry up.

477
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:50,980
Come here, it's comfortable.

478
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:56,280
What's up, Brother Jun? Drinking alone?

479
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:57,280
You should have told me earlier.

480
00:23:57,280 --> 00:24:00,210
Wouldn't it be better to go home and make some dishes?

481
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,840
Come on, I'll drink with you.

482
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,380
Is that all you're having?

483
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:09,760
This is pretty strong.

484
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,080
Uncle Daqing

485
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:13,080
would pass out after one sip.

486
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:14,880
He can't hold his liquor.

487
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:17,720
There's something I don't understand.

488
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:18,200
What is it?

489
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:18,880
Among all the brothers,

490
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:20,800
you're closest to Uncle Daqing, right?

491
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:21,360
Right?

492
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:22,480
Then why

493
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:24,280
isn't he one of

494
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,810
the Eight Great Guardians?

495
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:27,480
He wasn't given the title?

496
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:28,480
He joined later.

497
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:29,840
Nine Great Guardians sounds good too.

498
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,120
Xiaolong, it's not what you think.

499
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:33,120
The Eight Great Guardians is a title in the martial world.

500
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:34,000
It can't be changed?

501
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:34,440
You have to...

502
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:36,160
For example, the Four Heavenly Kings of Hong Kong.

503
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,080
If they announced the Five Heavenly Kings,

504
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:38,480
wouldn't that be ridiculous?

505
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:41,000
Please welcome Andy Lau from Hong Kong, China,

506
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:41,840
Jacky Cheung,

507
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,760
Leon Lai,

508
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:43,420
Aaron Kwok,

509
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:44,810
and Xiao Jun.

510
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:46,920
I think it's great.

511
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,980
You are the Heavenly King in my heart.

512
00:24:52,840 --> 00:24:53,400
Dad.

513
00:24:57,840 --> 00:24:58,640
What's wrong?

514
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:03,840
Heartburn.

515
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:08,100
Stop drinking if you have heartburn.

516
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:11,290
It hasn't been easy for you in there these past few years.

517
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:20,010
No, I think it hasn't been easy for you either.

518
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:22,480
You've been through so much growing up.

519
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,120
I completely...

520
00:25:23,120 --> 00:25:24,050
I completely...

521
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:25,480
I was still...

522
00:25:26,040 --> 00:25:27,640
I was still there with you...

523
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,360
All right.

524
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:42,920
Why are we both crying?

525
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:47,600
Why are we crying like this here?

526
00:25:47,600 --> 00:25:48,160
Really.

527
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:49,040
Exactly.

528
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:52,520
Didn't you just say Xiao Jun of the Five Heavenly Kings?

529
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:55,560
Well, how about the Heavenly King sings you a song?

530
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:00,680
Once loved deeply.

531
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:03,840
Once felt helpless.

532
00:26:04,760 --> 00:26:06,640
Once shed tears,

533
00:26:07,120 --> 00:26:08,840
reluctant to let go.

534
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,840
Once was young.

535
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:15,000
Once was impulsive.

536
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:21,320
Once got drunk for you.

537
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:40,200
Look at you.

538
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,600
You look great.

539
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:42,320
Brother.

540
00:26:43,120 --> 00:26:44,280
Your hair is all white.

541
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:46,240
At my age, of course it's white.

542
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,000
They are all waiting at the restaurant.

543
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:59,120
Get in the car. I'll take you there. Come on.

544
00:26:59,120 --> 00:26:59,760
Brother.

545
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,490
I plan to live a different life.

546
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:10,560
Alright.

547
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:12,400
Live a different life. Alright.

548
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:13,930
I'm leaving then, brother.

549
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:33,320
Come here, everyone.

550
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:35,040
Let me introduce two new colleagues to you.

551
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:36,170
Let's welcome them.

552
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,400
Please introduce yourselves.

553
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:40,080
Hello, everyone. My name is Lan Lingling.

554
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:41,410
You can call me Xiao Lan.

555
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:42,880
It's my first day working here.

556
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:43,920
I hope to learn a lot from you all.

557
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:44,520
Bowen.

558
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:44,880
Chao.

559
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:47,040
Lawyer Li is looking for you.

560
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:52,740
This day has finally come.

561
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:54,520
Come in.

562
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:55,880
Lawyer Li.

563
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:56,800
Sit down.

564
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:00,620
Have a seat.

565
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:02,480
I have something to tell you.

566
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:06,520
Sit down.

567
00:28:06,520 --> 00:28:07,120
Lawyer Li.

568
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,060
I want to say a few words first.

569
00:28:10,520 --> 00:28:12,080
I've been a chatterbox since I was a kid.

570
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,160
My mom used to beat me for it.

571
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:14,290
But I never changed.

572
00:28:14,320 --> 00:28:15,560
I also love a bit of gossip.

573
00:28:15,560 --> 00:28:16,280
When you were away,

574
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:17,610
I sat in your chair once.

575
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:18,920
But I really don't have any bad intentions.

576
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:20,200
Since I joined the team,

577
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:22,000
All I want is to handle cases every day.

578
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:23,440
I just want the best for our team.

579
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:25,570
And my phone is on silent every day now.

580
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:27,280
I don't want to leave.

581
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:30,600
Sit down.

582
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:39,800
Who said you two could leave?

583
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:44,160
No, we both know.

584
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:45,840
We are the leftovers.

585
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:47,440
We had a farewell dinner that day,

586
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:50,320
and then so many new people came to the firm.

587
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:53,080
I was wondering why you two

588
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,200
have been showing off

589
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,800
in front of me recently.

590
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:58,320
I treated you to dinner to reward you

591
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,200
for your hard work recently.

592
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,960
Do you have so little confidence in yourselves,

593
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:03,820
or do you have no confidence in me?

594
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:04,800
We do.

595
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:05,720
We have confidence.

596
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,760
Anyway, I have a lot of confidence in myself.

597
00:29:07,760 --> 00:29:09,280
No matter who joins my team,

598
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:10,320
I can lead them well.

599
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:11,120
Of course.

600
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:12,440
You two

601
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:14,080
have saved me a lot of energy.

602
00:29:14,360 --> 00:29:16,560
So a good team doesn't depend on the number of people.

603
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:18,890
I didn't plan to add any new people either.

604
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:19,800
What did I tell you?

605
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:21,280
I said we are the apples of his eye.

606
00:29:21,280 --> 00:29:22,240
You just overthink things.

607
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:24,040
Didn't you tell me at dinner that day

608
00:29:24,040 --> 00:29:24,480
that...

609
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:24,960
Come in.

610
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:26,760
Mr. Li.

611
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:29,220
A client specifically asked for you.

612
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:31,840
No appointment, but insists on seeing you now.

613
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:34,160
Did they say what the case is about?

614
00:29:34,160 --> 00:29:35,000
They didn't say anything,

615
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:36,660
just that they want to see you.

616
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:43,120
Son.

617
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:45,040
Mom.

618
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:53,040
Mom.

619
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,320
You came back so suddenly

620
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,200
without telling me.

621
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:57,480
I could have at least picked you up at the airport.

622
00:29:57,480 --> 00:29:59,140
I just wanted to surprise you.

623
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:00,560
A senior partner's

624
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:01,560
office

625
00:30:01,560 --> 00:30:02,820
is indeed impressive.

626
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:04,490
The view is really nice too.

627
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:07,120
You came back so suddenly.

628
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:09,760
Is something wrong?

629
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:12,200
I just happened to have a few days off,

630
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:13,680
and I missed you,

631
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,920
so I came back to spend some time with you.

632
00:30:15,920 --> 00:30:16,400
Okay.

633
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:20,240
If he's free today, let me treat your Director Wang to a meal.

634
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:21,770
I want to thank him in person

635
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:23,330
for taking good care of you.

636
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:24,960
Our director is very busy.

637
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:26,560
Even busy people have to eat.

638
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:28,720
Ma'am,

639
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:30,800
please have some tea.

640
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:32,040
Thank you. Thanks.

641
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,560
You're so sweet.

642
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,720
Are you Xin's colleague?

643
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,840
Yes, ma'am. I'm his mentee.

644
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:39,360
Mom, Mom.

645
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,560
We're working.

646
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:42,520
Why don't you go home and wait for me?

647
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:43,320
All right.

648
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:44,800
I'll go home and wait for you then.

649
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:46,200
Come back early.

650
00:30:46,320 --> 00:30:47,440
With your back injury,

651
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:48,120
you shouldn't overwork yourself.

652
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:48,920
Got it?

653
00:30:48,920 --> 00:30:49,800
Okay, I got it.

654
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:50,720
I'll call a car for you.

655
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:51,920
I can call one for her.

656
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:52,760
You go ahead with your work.

657
00:30:52,760 --> 00:30:53,520
Ma'am, I'll walk you out.

658
00:30:53,520 --> 00:30:54,440
Okay.

659
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:56,060
I'll head back now.

660
00:30:56,320 --> 00:30:57,800
Send me a WeChat when you get home.

661
00:30:57,800 --> 00:30:58,480
Okay.

662
00:30:58,560 --> 00:30:59,280
Hello, Ma'am.

663
00:30:59,280 --> 00:30:59,720
Hello.

664
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:00,600
This way, Ma'am.

665
00:31:00,600 --> 00:31:01,360
Right this way.

666
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:02,520
Ma'am, you look so young.

667
00:31:02,520 --> 00:31:03,520
I couldn't tell at all

668
00:31:03,520 --> 00:31:05,080
that you are Lawyer Li's mother.

669
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:06,520
Standing next to him, you look like siblings.

670
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:06,920
Yes.

671
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:08,380
Look at how well you speak.

672
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:12,360
Thank you guys for coming into the live stream.

673
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:12,760
Yi***: Welcome, welcome. Leyang's new streamer makes a grand debut.

674
00:31:12,760 --> 00:31:13,520
What's this English name?

675
00:31:13,520 --> 00:31:14,280
I don't know it.

676
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:15,810
This English word of yours,

677
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:17,440
anyway, welcome.

678
00:31:17,720 --> 00:31:19,000
Welcome, these letters.

679
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:19,920
This is my first time.

680
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:21,440
My first time streaming.

681
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:22,600
I'm Xiao Jun,

682
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:24,520
one of the Eight Great Guardians of Leyang.

683
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:26,200
Some of the older folks in Leyang

684
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:27,600
might know me.

685
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:29,320
A while ago,

686
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:32,000
a really good brother of mine

687
00:31:32,280 --> 00:31:33,040
passed away.

688
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:34,480
Passed away.

689
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:36,520
And suddenly,

690
00:31:37,320 --> 00:31:38,440
I just understood.

691
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:39,720
I said, while I'm still alive,

692
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:41,360
I must leave myself

693
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,120
a memorial.

694
00:31:43,600 --> 00:31:44,480
So I...

695
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:45,400
Here comes another one.

696
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,600
Welcome, Li Guochen.

697
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:48,600
Li... Li Guochen.

698
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:55,760
Speaking of Li Guochen,

699
00:31:55,760 --> 00:31:58,040
you have the same name as a cop I know.

700
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:01,760
Where is Tietou?

701
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:03,440
He did practice the Iron Head skill,

702
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:05,520
but his master might be a charlatan.

703
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,760
Every time he goes out to fight,

704
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:08,520
this Tietou,

705
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:09,800
his head definitely gets busted open.

706
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:11,060
Morning, Sister Long.

707
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:12,410
Morning, Director.

708
00:32:14,520 --> 00:32:15,520
You look comfortable.

709
00:32:15,520 --> 00:32:16,520
Found a new desk?

710
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,120
Just to be closer to you.

711
00:32:18,120 --> 00:32:19,800
Why do you need to be close to me?

712
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:22,520
Being closer to you means being closer to the AC.

713
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:24,120
It's so hot outside.

714
00:32:24,320 --> 00:32:25,440
What are you watching?

715
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:26,440
Following a star?

716
00:32:27,440 --> 00:32:28,440
Following my dad?

717
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:30,040
He speaks so well.

718
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:31,800
What? Are you changing careers?

719
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:33,800
I was thinking your dad is gaining followers fast.

720
00:32:33,800 --> 00:32:35,240
He's about to become an influencer.

721
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:37,500
I'll ask him to help promote our law firm.

722
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:38,800
Come on.

723
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:39,960
Turn it off.

724
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,020
Someone's coming.

725
00:32:41,120 --> 00:32:41,960
A client?

726
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:43,280
Come in.

727
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:45,680
Hello, hello, hello.

728
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:47,120
I'm the marketing manager of this law firm.

729
00:32:47,120 --> 00:32:48,580
What do you need advice on?

730
00:32:48,600 --> 00:32:49,000
I...

731
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:50,800
You can ask anyone around here.

732
00:32:50,800 --> 00:32:52,960
Our Lawyer Xiao can handle any case.

733
00:32:52,960 --> 00:32:53,280
I know. I...

734
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:54,000
The lawyer is inside.

735
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:54,720
She'll be out in a minute.

736
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:55,520
Jia'er.

737
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:57,360
Coming.

738
00:32:57,520 --> 00:32:58,280
Sister Zhao.

739
00:32:58,840 --> 00:32:59,840
I hope I'm not interrupting your work.

740
00:32:59,840 --> 00:33:00,400
Not at all.

741
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:01,640
Don't be so polite.

742
00:33:03,120 --> 00:33:05,040
Lawyer Xiao, would you do me the honor

743
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:06,280
of having a meal with me?

744
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:07,210
Sure, let's eat.

745
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:09,080
But since you're on my turf, it's my treat.

746
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:10,280
No, no, no. I arranged it,

747
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:11,000
so it's my treat.

748
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:11,720
Then you treat.

749
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:12,450
You're rich.

750
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:13,640
Let's go.

751
00:33:13,640 --> 00:33:14,680
Bye, Sister Zhao.

752
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:15,480
What are we eating?

753
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:16,240
You choose.

754
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:19,760
What's up, Brother Hu?

755
00:33:19,760 --> 00:33:21,040
You thought it was a big client?

756
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:22,720
That's Sister Long's high school classmate.

757
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:23,840
What are you laughing at?

758
00:33:23,840 --> 00:33:24,800
This is my professional instinct

759
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,440
as a marketing manager.

760
00:33:26,720 --> 00:33:27,520
I'm so sharp.

761
00:33:27,520 --> 00:33:28,920
I just reacted in a flash.

762
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:30,440
Uncle, be a little modest.

763
00:33:30,720 --> 00:33:32,240
When Lawyer Li came last time,

764
00:33:32,240 --> 00:33:33,720
you also thought he was a big client.

765
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:35,000
That was so awkward.

766
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,720
Why bring it up if you know it's awkward?

767
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:37,440
Mr. Wang,

768
00:33:37,440 --> 00:33:39,720
the proposal for the client is being revised.

769
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,450
Don't worry.

770
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:42,240
Wait a moment.

771
00:33:43,040 --> 00:33:45,520
Liu, send me the revised proposal ASAP.

772
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:47,160
Check it a few times before sending.

773
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:48,820
Don't make any more mistakes.

774
00:33:50,280 --> 00:33:53,360
That's why they say serious women are the most attractive.

775
00:33:53,360 --> 00:33:54,280
Not bad,

776
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:55,600
Zhao.

777
00:33:56,120 --> 00:33:57,040
Got promoted.

778
00:33:57,280 --> 00:33:58,360
Got rich.

779
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:00,520
I'm still just a corporate slave.

780
00:34:00,520 --> 00:34:01,600
Unlike you,

781
00:34:01,880 --> 00:34:04,120
running a law firm and being your own boss.

782
00:34:04,120 --> 00:34:05,050
So much freedom.

783
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:06,200
I really wish

784
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:08,120
I had financial freedom like you.

785
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:09,600
Alright.

786
00:34:09,719 --> 00:34:12,920
You're so busy but still asked me out for a meal. What's up?

787
00:34:22,639 --> 00:34:25,120
Cheng Fei said he wants a divorce.

788
00:34:29,679 --> 00:34:30,340
Did you guys

789
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:33,600
have a fight?

790
00:34:34,520 --> 00:34:35,480
No, we didn't.

791
00:34:35,760 --> 00:34:37,120
There were no signs.

792
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:38,560
He just

793
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:41,800
suddenly and calmly said

794
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:44,000
we're incompatible.

795
00:34:44,120 --> 00:34:45,199
What do you mean incompatible?

796
00:34:45,199 --> 00:34:46,520
You've been fine for over ten years.

797
00:34:46,520 --> 00:34:48,650
How can you suddenly be incompatible?

798
00:34:50,719 --> 00:34:52,650
Has he been acting strange lately?

799
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:56,520
I've been on business trips for the past six months.

800
00:34:56,520 --> 00:34:58,760
I haven't been home much.

801
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:00,120
Even when I am home,

802
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:02,940
I barely speak a few words to him a day.

803
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:05,290
Acting strange?

804
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:08,800
Could he be acting out to get your attention?

805
00:35:09,120 --> 00:35:09,960
Really?

806
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,040
Rebelling against you in such an extreme way

807
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:14,100
is just to get more of your attention.

808
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:15,480
You've been together for over ten years.

809
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:17,340
You can't just break up like that.

810
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:21,520
Yeah.

811
00:35:25,880 --> 00:35:26,640
[Unlocked]

812
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:28,280
Hi, Mom.

813
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:30,120
Look what I made.

814
00:35:30,520 --> 00:35:31,880
It's a dinosaur.

815
00:35:32,040 --> 00:35:33,280
Yes, look.

816
00:35:33,720 --> 00:35:35,800
Jeffrey, your brother is here.

817
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:37,120
Do you remember him?

818
00:35:38,520 --> 00:35:39,280
Hello.

819
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:42,800
I miss you. When are you coming back?

820
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:43,920
I miss you too.

821
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:45,440
Be a good boy, okay?

822
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:46,280
Okay.

823
00:35:46,360 --> 00:35:48,160
Alright, I'll talk to you later.

824
00:35:48,280 --> 00:35:49,080
Love you.

825
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:54,080
Son.

826
00:35:54,600 --> 00:35:55,080
Well,

827
00:35:55,080 --> 00:35:56,000
have you eaten?

828
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:57,360
I've eaten.

829
00:35:57,640 --> 00:35:58,280
Look.

830
00:35:58,480 --> 00:36:01,080
This is wild American ginseng I bought for you,

831
00:36:01,080 --> 00:36:02,920
and this is deer antler.

832
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:04,920
They're both good for your health.

833
00:36:04,920 --> 00:36:06,360
Remember to take them.

834
00:36:06,760 --> 00:36:07,440
Mom,

835
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:10,080
it's quite a hassle to carry these.

836
00:36:10,080 --> 00:36:11,610
You can buy them online now.

837
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:13,000
Buying online

838
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:15,730
isn't the same as me picking them out personally.

839
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:19,120
This is a gift from Wilson.

840
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:20,200
See if you like it.

841
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:24,560
Mom, I don't drink.

842
00:36:25,160 --> 00:36:26,090
Thank him for me.

843
00:36:27,440 --> 00:36:28,880
This foreigner,

844
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,480
I told him you don't drink,

845
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:31,920
but he insisted on packing it.

846
00:36:31,920 --> 00:36:33,080
You see,

847
00:36:33,200 --> 00:36:34,860
it's the thought that counts.

848
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:35,920
Then I...

849
00:36:37,080 --> 00:36:38,680
I have something to tell you.

850
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:42,280
Son.

851
00:36:43,360 --> 00:36:44,080
Well,

852
00:36:45,480 --> 00:36:47,440
I want to discuss something with you.

853
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:48,360
Go ahead.

854
00:36:50,120 --> 00:36:52,600
I want to apply for permanent residency.

855
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:54,880
A business visa is inconvenient.

856
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:58,040
Yeah, it's exhausting for you to travel back and forth.

857
00:36:58,640 --> 00:36:59,400
Just do it if you want.

858
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:00,530
It's your decision.

859
00:37:00,560 --> 00:37:02,760
I'm mainly thinking about your future.

860
00:37:02,880 --> 00:37:03,320
You know,

861
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:06,320
you can't stay in this small place forever, right?

862
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,560
I also found you

863
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,360
a really good rehab center.

864
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:11,480
It's specially... No, I...

865
00:37:11,480 --> 00:37:12,000
Mom,

866
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,280
I'm doing fine here.

867
00:37:29,680 --> 00:37:31,140
Let me take this call, Mom.

868
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:40,360
Hello.

869
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:43,000
When is your next rehab session?

870
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,000
Wednesday. Why?

871
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,880
Nothing, just checking in on you.

872
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:49,520
How about I go with you on Wednesday?

873
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,380
That's it. I'm hanging up.

874
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:52,640
You're going with me?

875
00:38:05,720 --> 00:38:06,980
Drink the ginseng tea.

876
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,940
It's arranged so neatly, Mom.

877
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:13,800
Where is my computer?

878
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:15,000
I put it in your bedroom.

879
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:17,440
You can't just pile all these things

880
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,570
on the dining table.

881
00:38:18,640 --> 00:38:18,920
Thanks, Mom.

882
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:19,320
Drink.

883
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:20,610
Drink up.

884
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:32,920
Who is it?

885
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:34,450
Your food delivery is here.

886
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,400
Delivery? Who ordered delivery?

887
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:41,720
Your delivery.

888
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:47,800
What are you doing?

889
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:49,600
Didn't you see a living person locked outside?

890
00:38:49,600 --> 00:38:50,800
Aren't you just the delivery?

891
00:38:50,800 --> 00:38:53,060
I am an inseparable part of the delivery.

892
00:38:56,920 --> 00:38:57,920
Drinking alone?

893
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:00,200
Just because Xiaoxin isn't back,

894
00:39:00,200 --> 00:39:01,000
you can't just make do like this.

895
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,920
Eating noodles with green onions.

896
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:04,680
You're really something.

897
00:39:07,560 --> 00:39:09,760
Haven't had a drink in a few days, right?

898
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:12,530
I get a big glass and you get a small cup?

899
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:14,800
That's more like it.

900
00:39:15,560 --> 00:39:16,280
After this glass,

901
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:18,010
we're officially reconciled.

902
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:19,440
What reconciliation?

903
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:21,370
You're forcing a reconciliation.

904
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:22,800
You...

905
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:25,880
I saw you sneak into my live stream.

906
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:27,280
I didn't go into your live stream.

907
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:28,920
But in your live stream,

908
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:30,280
just talk about your own stuff.

909
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:31,280
Don't drag me into it.

910
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:32,610
Look at you. Look at you.

911
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,200
You said you didn't.

912
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:33,800
You saw it all.

913
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:36,200
And you still say you didn't go into the live stream.

914
00:39:36,200 --> 00:39:38,060
I was just warning you in advance,

915
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:39,280
to nip it in the bud.

916
00:39:39,280 --> 00:39:40,440
I know you too well.

917
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:41,640
When you pass away,

918
00:39:41,640 --> 00:39:44,000
when you're cremated, your mouth

919
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:45,560
will have to be taken out and burned separately.

920
00:39:45,560 --> 00:39:46,400
It's too stubborn.

921
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:49,400
When you're cremated, your mouth

922
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:50,800
will have to be put in a separate box.

923
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:51,560
Why is that?

924
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:52,490
It's too chatty.

925
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:58,220
How come you have time to visit today?

926
00:39:58,800 --> 00:39:59,560
It's nothing.

927
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:01,920
I just came to see how he's recovering.

928
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,960
Li Lv is really lucky

929
00:40:04,520 --> 00:40:06,650
to have someone care about him so much.

930
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:07,920
Don't be nervous.

931
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:08,560
Steady.

932
00:40:08,560 --> 00:40:10,040
Don't sprain it again.

933
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:11,520
I won't. I'm fine.

934
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:14,000
Don't push yourself.

935
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:18,560
Zhao Jia got promoted recently.

936
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:20,280
He must be very busy.

937
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:21,420
Still the same.

938
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:24,800
Always on business trips. I never see her.

939
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:25,920
That won't do.

940
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:27,400
You must miss her a lot.

941
00:40:27,960 --> 00:40:29,360
I'm used to it.

942
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:32,000
Used to it? You can't get used to that.

943
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:32,800
If you ask me,

944
00:40:33,160 --> 00:40:34,080
Zhao Jia shouldn't

945
00:40:34,080 --> 00:40:36,810
work all the time. She needs a work-life balance.

946
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:39,610
Otherwise, Dr. Cheng will be so heartbroken.

947
00:40:41,640 --> 00:40:43,320
Change positions. Lie down.

948
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:50,210
Let's go camping this weekend.

949
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:51,760
I remember when you guys were dating,

950
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,280
you loved camping, right?

951
00:40:53,600 --> 00:40:55,800
Do you still have all that gear?

952
00:40:56,480 --> 00:40:57,360
Camping?

953
00:40:58,320 --> 00:40:59,600
Zhao Jia doesn't have time.

954
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:02,120
Come on, you can always make time.

955
00:41:02,120 --> 00:41:04,320
Don't worry about Zhao Jia. I'll handle her.

956
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:05,050
How about it?

957
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:07,820
What about you?

958
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:11,660
What do you mean? Weren't you listening?

959
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:12,400
Camping.

960
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:16,610
That's more like it.

961
00:41:17,080 --> 00:41:18,760
Then it's settled.

962
00:41:18,760 --> 00:41:19,960
You two bring Nuannuan,

963
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:20,920
and I'll bring him.

964
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:22,920
The five of us will relive our youth.

965
00:41:29,680 --> 00:41:30,720
Come catch me!

966
00:41:30,960 --> 00:41:33,160
You two put the things there. I'll do it.

967
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:36,200
Look who's here.

968
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:37,440
Nuannuan.

969
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:39,200
Little Nuannuan.

970
00:41:39,360 --> 00:41:40,920
Do you still remember who I am?

971
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:41,720
I remember.

972
00:41:41,720 --> 00:41:44,160
Auntie is a good friend of Mom and Dad.

973
00:41:44,160 --> 00:41:45,280
An old classmate.

974
00:41:45,440 --> 00:41:46,560
Hello, Auntie.

975
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:47,800
Hello, Uncle.

976
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:51,920
Did I say something wrong?

977
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:53,720
No, you said it perfectly.

978
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:54,760
Auntie, Uncle.

979
00:41:54,760 --> 00:41:55,960
Are they a good match?

980
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:56,800
They are.

981
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:57,720
See?

982
00:41:57,880 --> 00:41:59,600
Children have sharp eyes.

983
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:02,800
I'm pushing hard!

984
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:03,720
Sit tight!

985
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:05,280
Don't swing us off!

986
00:42:05,920 --> 00:42:08,560
We should take her out to play more often.

987
00:42:11,600 --> 00:42:12,320
Okay.

988
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:16,960
In the past,

989
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:18,780
it was my fault.

990
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,530
I could never find the time.

991
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:23,280
I'll make some adjustments from now on.

992
00:42:25,240 --> 00:42:25,920
It's fine.

993
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:28,200
Uncle,

994
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:29,600
I want to go take a look over there.

995
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:30,320
Over there?

996
00:42:30,560 --> 00:42:31,090
Let's go.

997
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:38,240
Mr. Wang.

998
00:42:38,720 --> 00:42:39,980
I'm not busy. Go ahead.

999
00:42:41,840 --> 00:42:44,360
Aunt, these are the flowers Uncle gave you.

1000
00:42:44,360 --> 00:42:46,160
Flowers from Uncle?

1001
00:42:46,160 --> 00:42:49,090
Then I should thank Nuannuan for bringing them to me.

1002
00:42:52,720 --> 00:42:53,640
Uncle.

1003
00:42:54,040 --> 00:42:54,960
No need to be so polite.
